  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 522.03 Application Requirements for Agricultural Projects",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 522.03 Application Requirements for Agricultural Projects. The project-specific information required by Env-Wt 310.01(c)(1) or Env-Wt 311.03(b)(11), as applicable, for an agricultural project shall be as follows:\n\n(a) A conservation plan prepared by NRCS, a county conservation district or a plan of conservation practices for proposed wetland impacts prepared by a certified wetland scientist;\n\n(b) Aerial photography with site impact located;\n\n(c) NRCS soil survey reports for the project area;\n\n(d) A wetland delineation and impact plan prepared by an NRCS soil scientist or certified wetland scientist;\n\n(e) A sediment and erosion control plan;\n\n(f) A construction sequence detailing timing of the work proposed, including dewatering plans, construction of access routes, and temporary impacts; and\n\n(g) All of the information and documentation specified in Env-Wt 522.06(a).\n\nSource. #12805, eff 12-15-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt500.html"
